WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:10.559
Education reformers love education
technology. This has been true for a long

00:00:10.559 --> 00:00:15.870
time. The radio, the TV, the desktop computer:
each was going to revolutionize

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:21.420
schooling. Guess what: They didn't.
Technology is a powerful tool, and like

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:25.890
any tool what matters is how we use it.
We have to use it right and that means

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:30.660
understanding why it matters. Technology
is great at offering access. For kids in

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:34.110
rural schools, who don't have access to
advanced placement classes, online

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:38.190
delivery of courses can make all the
difference. Technology is great at

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:42.750
supporting personalization. For teachers
with 25 kids, it can be hard to tend to

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:46.860
the needs of each and every one.
Computerized assessments can make a huge

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:51.059
difference. But iPads aren't going to
eliminate the need for teachers. Kids

00:00:51.059 --> 00:00:55.739
need role models, mentors, and a kick in
the pants. Technology can't do any of

00:00:55.739 --> 00:00:59.969
that. But technology can make a huge
difference. It can help teachers do their

00:00:59.969 --> 00:01:06.300
job better, and it can support kids as
they learn. And honestly, that's more than enough.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:10.340
To learn more about my take on
education technology, check the links in

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:14.549
the description below. Also, let us know
what other topics you'd like a AEI

00:01:14.549 --> 00:01:18.619
scholars to cover in 60 seconds.

